OL,3,ASurge in AI-assisted complaints putting
OL,4,Aextra strain on councils and schools
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rising tide of complaints written
OL,7,Fwith the help of AI is substantially
OL,8,Fincreasing the workload of schools,
OL,9,Flocal councils and other public bodies,
OL,10,Fthe BBC has been told.
OL,12,FChatbots can produce complex arguments,
OL,13,Foften quoting regulations or acts of
OL,14,FParliament, with documents running to
OL,15,Fdozens of pages long.
OL,17,FOne body said complaints once contained
OL,18,Fto a single sheet of A4 could now run
OL,19,Fto 20 pages. They said AI also made
OL,20,Ferrors and sometimes misquoted
OL,21,Flegislation, and further added to the
OL,22,Ftime it takes to deal with grievances.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
